**How to implement.** The pull and the update proved end to end over the real adapter and the real library database: a fixture snapshot under the test output and SQLite `:memory:` (the S13.1 brief 'Tests over a fixture snapshot: search; a pull gives version 1 with provenance; an unchanged update makes no new version; a changed record gives version 2'; .spec-md §9 'Each library proxy's suite runs against BOTH the in-memory store and SQLite :memory:'; .spec-md §3.9). Tests only; no product file changes. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourcePullSqliteTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourcePullSqliteTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, its module doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. Each fact opens `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), disposed at its end, composes its import context as `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase <the database>)` (step 95) and its material store as `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase <the database>` (step 69), and builds the adapter as `MaterialSourceProxy.createRefractiveIndexInfo` (step 447) over `MaterialSourceFixture.freshSources "MaterialSourcePullSqliteTests"`, whose snapshot `writeSnapshot` writes with `siPage ()`, a `copyingDownloader` of an archive `writeArchive` writes beside it, and `fixedClock` of 2026-11-04; nothing reaches the network. `a pulled refractiveindex.info page is a user material at version 1 with its provenance and its pulled-source row`: `searchRecords (MaterialSourceQuery "silicon")` finds `main/Si/nk/Test.yml`; `pullRecord` of it (step 444) answers one `PullAddedEntry` at version 1; the material store's `tryGetMaterial` of its id resolves a material named `Si (Silicon), Test 2026: n,k 0.25–0.70 µm` whose physics is the page's import; the import seam's `tryLatestEnvelope` holds `SourcePullProvenance` with the record, `2026-11-01`, `CC0-1.0`, the citation and the page file's hash, its protection `UserManaged`; the database's `PulledSources` table (read through `run`) holds exactly one row, of that entry at version 1 with those texts; and `attributionLinesOf` of the entry (step 114) answers `Si (Silicon), Test 2026: n,k 0.25–0.70 µm: Licence CC0-1.0`. `an update whose page is unchanged mints no version`: after that pull, `updateSourceSnapshot` (step 444) with the archive of `siPage ()` answers `SourceRefreshed` whose snapshot is `2026-11-04` and whose one pull is `PullFoundUnchanged` at version 1; `resolveVersion` of version 2 answers `None`; and `PulledSources` still holds one row. `an update whose page changed mints version 2 and keeps version 1`: after that pull, the update with the archive of `changedSiPage ()` answers `PullMintedVersion` at version 2; version 2 resolves with the changed page's import as its physics (n 3.790 at 0.70 µm) under the same name, its provenance `2026-11-04` and the changed page's hash; version 1 resolves as before, through `resolveVersion`; the material's latest is version 2; and `PulledSources` holds two rows, versions 1 and 2. `pulling the same page twice writes it once`: a second `pullRecord` answers `PullFoundUnchanged` at version 1, and the entry holds one version.

**Acceptance.** After the end-to-end facts land, a pulled refractiveindex.info page MUST be a user material at version 1 in the SQLite library with its pull provenance and its pulled-source row, an update of an unchanged page MUST mint nothing and an update of a changed page MUST mint version 2 and keep version 1; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a pulled refractiveindex.info page is a user material at version 1 with its provenance and its pulled-source row`, `an update whose page is unchanged mints no version`, `an update whose page changed mints version 2 and keeps version 1` and `pulling the same page twice writes it once`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
